There are exactly 28 chips on the field. The squares covered by the same chip are marked by the same letter, different chips are marked by different letters. It is guaranteed that the field's description is correct.\n\nIt is also guaranteed that at least one solution exists.\n\n## Output\n\nPrint on the first line the number of ways to replace chips with dominoes to get a magic figure. That is the total number of contests that can be won using this arrangement of the chips. Next n lines containing m characters each, should contain a field from dots and numbers from 0 to 6 ΓÇö any of the possible solutions. All dominoes should be different.\n\n## Examples\n\nExample 1:\n```\n8 8\n.aabbcc.\n.defghi.\nkdefghij\nklmnopqj\n.lmnopq.\n.rstuvw.\nxrstuvwy\nxzzAABBy\n```\n```\n10080\n.001122.\n.001122.\n33440055\n33440055\n.225566.\n.225566.\n66113344\n66113344\n```","type":"text"}],"contestId":97,"index":"A","memoryLimit":"256 megabytes","name":"Domino","problemKey":"97-A","rating":null,"tags":[],"timeLimit":"0.5 second","url":"https://codeforces.com/contest/97/problem/A"},{"approaches":[{"label":"Approach 1","number":1,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 2","number":2,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 3","number":3,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 4","number":4,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 5","number":5,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 6","number":6,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 7","number":7,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 8","number":8,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 9","number":9,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"App